{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790403634,"nonce":"Q7/8rxibL4JQM2IA96NO9P/BJ8c=","message":"method_call investigation (NUC, 85c6065; CI ratio 4.6-5.0x, NUC 0.023 vs LuaJIT 0.0056-0.0067).\n\nSteady state is not the gap: at 1M iterations the Cranelift-only build runs about 2 ns per call, LuaJIT about 1. At the benchmark's 100k it is warm-up.\n\nSplit: the Toggle loop alone takes 6.2 ms, the NthToggle loop alone 15.0 ms, both 22.5 ms. Timeline of the full run: module baseline compile 0.8-4.2 ms (interpreter meanwhile), first optimised compile 4.8-9.3 ms. Loop 1's ten activate.value pairs are MIR-inlined and collapse to one guard, a field read and a field write. Loop 2 had not run at that compile, so it is cold: generic wren_call_0 at ~17 ns/call until the cold-loop recompile (~9-10 ms, MIR ~1.2 ms) installs around 19-21 ms.\n\nProfile of the cold window (recompile disabled, 400k): wren_call_0_inner 33%, dispatch_call_rooted 26%, record_call 12%, AUTO_DEOPT_RETRY TLS HashMap lookup ~6%, module_vars_for 4%, propose_top_tier 2%; the callee body 5%.\n\nTried and rejected:\n- Plant a polymorphic entry (kind 1|IC_POLYMORPHIC) from CHA on empty sites with 2-3 implementors, so the loop is not cold and Cranelift dispatches over the hierarchy at once. 100k: 0.0233 -\u003e 0.0205; but the hierarchy code never fills caches, so the loop never gets the monomorphic recompile: 400k 0.040 -\u003e 0.056, 1M 0.075 -\u003e 0.093 (Cranelift-only 0.057 -\u003e 0.115). Net loss.\n- Single-pass regalloc for optimised compiles: method_call 0.0243 -\u003e 0.0220, recompile 8.7 -\u003e 7.3 ms, but mandelbrot +37%, long method_call runs +15-34%.\n- Skip the AUTO_DEOPT_RETRY map when empty (global pending count): no measurable change.\n- Disabling Cranelift-level callee inlining: baseline compile 5.3 -\u003e 4.8 ms, no gain.\n\nOptions with real payoff, all larger pieces of work:\n1. Cold loop dispatched over the hierarchy while still recording what it sees (the hierarchy's hit path stores the site's cache once), then recompiled: cold window ~3x faster calls, steady state kept.\n2. Recompile only the region a cold loop header reaches (an OSR-only body) instead of the whole function: for method_call, roughly half the recompile.\n3. Cut first-tier latency (baseline compile of the module body 2.8-3.4 ms; interpreter ~50 ns/call before it).","files":null}]}